  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If the maximum load carried by an elevator is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mtext>-Passengers</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mtext>-elevator</mtext><mo>)</mo></math> , which is moving up with a uniform speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and the frictional force acting on it is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>, then the maximum power used by the motor is _____________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kW</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "48",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"assets\\st0046_aef433ab1be7.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 195px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The maximum force acting is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>14000</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2000</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>16000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p>The formula for power is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mi>v</mi></math>.</p><p>It is given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>16000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>48000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kW</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kW</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}